.SH NAME
.PP
Stp \- STP service process object
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
\f[B]var stp = new Stp([hostname],[svcname])\f[]
.SH CATEGORY
.PP
Stp
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
This function is used to create a new STP service process object to connect to
STP nodes.
.SH PARAMETERS
.IP \[bu] 2
hostname ( \f[I]string, optional\f[] )
.PP
The hostname of the host where the target STP is located.
.IP \[bu] 2
svcname ( \f[I]number/string, optional\f[] )
.PP
The port used by the target STP, the default port is 9622.
.SH RETURN VALUE
.PP
When the function executes successfully, it will return an object of Stp.
.PP
When the function fails, an exception will be thrown and an error message will
be printed.
.SH ERRORS
.PP
